// The parser bounds how deeply an expression may nest, and says so once.
//
// A recursive descent parser has a stack, and source that is broken in this
// particular way would exhaust it -- so the bound is stated rather than
// discovered, and the report names the limit instead of describing a crash.
// Reported once rather than at every level, because a thousand frames each
// naming the brace they could not find describe one mistake a thousand times.
